WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
[THEME MUSIC]

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:01.900
[COFFEE POURING]

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:06.180
[THEME MUSIC]

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.450
 What's up, everyone?

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.470
This is "Disney+ Deets,"
where we break down everything

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.010
you need to know about
your favorite Disney+

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.600
movies and series.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.400
I'm Kenneth--

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.680
MARCELLUS: And I'm Marcellus,
and not to toot our own horns,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.390
but we're pretty
much the biggest

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.190
Disney+ fans out there.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.260
 No, let's do it!

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.240
Toot toot!

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.050
Beep beep!

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:23.850
That's right!

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.720
 Let's get into it.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.600
[THEME MUSIC]

00:00:30.443 --> 00:00:32.310
KENNETH: Today, we're telling
you what you need to know,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.020
and what you maybe
didn't know about Marvel

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.790
Studios' "Black Panther."

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.710
Like so many of
you out there, Marcellus and 

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.020
I have been really
devastated over the loss

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.090
of the great Chadwick Boseman.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.760
Who, of course, brought
the Black Panther to life.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.500
MARCELLUS: Yes,
Ken, his performance

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.850
was everything to me.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.650
He embodied the
character so well.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.630
It was really a joy to watch.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.240
KENNETH: When Chadwick Boseman
first appears on screen,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.880
it's literally the embodiment
of Wakanda walking before you.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:58.680
MARCELLUS: Yeah.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.080
KENNETH: I remember
sitting in the theater

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.470
and I just got chills.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.850
Of course, I was
in my African garb,

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.400
and I just wanted to
rise up in the theater.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.920
But, I want to say
this, Chadwick Boseman

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.750
will always be missed,
and we're so happy that we

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.050
have this piece of him--
MARCELLUS: Yeah.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:11.950
KENNETH: --on film forever.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:12.960
MARCELLUS: I agree, Ken.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.670
And we want to pay
tribute to Chadwick

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.370
and celebrate all the
talent and hard work

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.650
that went into the making
of this great film.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.730
KENNETH: Yes, sir.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.417
So give us some history of
the characters, Marcellus.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:25.350
MARCELLUS: The Black Panther
character first appeared over

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:29.430
50 years ago, in "Fantastic
Four" Volume 1, Issue 52,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.350
published in 1966.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.660
His first appearance in the
Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.590
however, was in 2016's
"Captain America: Civil War."

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.350
KENNETH: Chadwick Boseman
is perfect for this.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.210
Nate Moore, the film's
executive producer,

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.950
said that Chadwick read
all the comic books,

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.370
he came to him with
questions, and he had

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.650
his own ideas about Wakanda.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.240
He was not taking
anything for granted

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.830
and was fully
invested in the role.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.450
MARCELLUS: You really feel that.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.390
This film is directed and
co-written by Ryan Coogler,

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.230
and, Ken, I'm obsessed.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:01.000
I really admire him.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.250
KENNETH: This is
his third feature

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.810
film with Michael B.
Jordan, who portrays

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.040
Killmonger in the film.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.890
Jordan has said that Black
Panther was a character he'd

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.580
look up to his entire life.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.480
Ugh, the Dora Milaje.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.280
MARCELLUS: Oh.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.100
KENNETH: They are Wakanda's
all-female special force

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.930
unit, led by Danai Gurira,
also known as Okoye.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.085
MARCELLUS: Shout
out to you, Danai.

00:02:23.085 --> 00:02:24.330
[APPLAUSE]
KENNETH: Girl power.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.350
I'm not mad about it.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.720
MARCELLUS: To fill the ranks
of this elite security force,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.730
the filmmakers and stunt team
met with hundreds of women,

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.330
including film and
television stunt players,

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.760
track and field athletes,
dancers, and MMA fighters.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.560
KENNETH: Mm-hmm.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.330
MARCELLUS: Listen, they were
not to be toyed with at all.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.220
KENNETH: The main cast
spent three months training

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.140
for the demanding
action in the film,

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.680
mostly doing their own stunts.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.140
MARCELLUS: Yes, you
can really tell.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.240
KENNETH: The cast and
stunt team also practiced

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.370
with African drums so
their movements would have

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.850
a musical quality that's found
in many African-based martial

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.110
arts styles.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.180
It's just the
rhythm and the soul.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.050
KENNETH: [LAUGHS] Yes.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.260
Winston Duke plays
M'Baku, and this was

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.580
his first major motion picture.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.380
[M'BAKU CHANT]

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.510
KENNETH: Exactly, we were
all sitting in a theater,

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:07.980
but after that chant
everyone wanted

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.540
to stand up to attention.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.440
[MIMICS M'BAKU CHANT]

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.240
MARCELLUS: Yeah.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.810
KENNETH: He was great.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.390
Oh my God, look at Wakanda!

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.290
MARCELLUS: Yes.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.330
KENNETH: Ryan Coogler
brought on production

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.180
designer, Hannah Beachler,
to bring the world of Wakanda

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.420
to life.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.720
So Wakanda's main
resource is the metal

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.720
known as Vibranium, right?

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:26.520
MARCELLUS: Right.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.080
KENNETH: Biechler wanted
to incorporate that

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.470
into her designs as
much as possible.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:30.270
MARCELLUS: Yeah.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.240
KENNETH: She even went to
mining and metallurgy experts

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.420
to determine what the different
phases of Vibranium could be.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.160
MARCELLUS: Ken, you lost me.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.310
KENNETH: I almost lost myself.

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.770
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.110
MARCELLUS: Ken, look
at this, the Warrior

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.620
Falls set is one of the most
impressive in the film.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.420
KENNETH: Yeah.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.540
MARCELLUS: It was inspired
by the real life Oribi Gorge

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.620
in South Africa.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.950
KENNETH: The massive set, built
on a back lot north of Atlanta,

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.050
clocked in at what--
120 by 75 feet?

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:56.850
MARCELLUS: What?

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.490
KENNETH: With practical
cliff faces 30 feet tall.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.720
Now, instead of actual rock,

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.520
MARCELLUS: Mm-hmm.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.960
KENNETH: Over 25,000 cubic feet
of foam was used for the set.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.520
The bottom of the challenge pool
was padded for the stunt team.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.320
MARCELLUS: OK.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.930
KENNETH: But was painted
to look like rock.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.110
The filmmaking team also
engineered a fully functional

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:19.380
flowing waterfall and pool
at the ledge of the cliff

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:25.080
with six pumps feeding
over 125,000 gallons of

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.047
temperature-controlled water.

00:04:26.047 --> 00:04:26.847
MARCELLUS: Oh, wow.

00:04:26.847 --> 00:04:27.720
KENNETH: Doing what?

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.120
Piping up through the set
at a rate of how much?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.720
I'm glad you asked,
30,000 gallons per minute.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.160
Before doing what?

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.050
Recirculating
through the system!

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:39.630
MARCELLUS: Ken, I probably
would try to go swimming.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.780
KENNETH: [LAUGHS]
You would, you would.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.110
MARCELLUS: [LAUGHS]
Just swimming.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.240
Yes, this part right here.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.340
This chase sequence
was filmed on location

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.160
in the actual streets
of Busan, South Korea.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.900
KENNETH: I want you
to realize, the way

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.340
they driving in this scene--
MARCELLUS: Yeah.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.390
KENNETH: --is how
my mama was driving

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.830
trying to get me to school
when we missed the bus.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.880
MARCELLUS: Oh, I understand.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:57.870
KENNETH: [LAUGHS]

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.180
MARCELLUS: And you know what
I really notice in this?

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.100
Ryan Coogler wanted
the South Korea

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.090
action sequence to be seamless.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.060
So he had an editor
on set cutting

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:08.280
footage in real
time, which isn't

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.810
usually done during production.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.700
But Coogler felt
it was the best way

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.970
to capture all the action,
stunts, and special effects

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.770
in the frame, on time.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:19.645
Wakanda is a modern society
that's deeply in touch

00:05:19.645 --> 00:05:20.760
with its history.
KENNETH: Mm-hmm.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.470
MARCELLUS: You can see it
especially in this set.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:25.180
It's sleek and modern, with
visual effects, enhancements.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:25.980
KENNETH: Mm-hmm.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.840
MARCELLUS: But then,
under the high-tech glass

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.220
floor is an ancient ruin--

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.020
KENNETH: I saw that.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.360
MARCELLUS: --on the metal
columns of the room,

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:37.270
you can find script written in
5th century Nigerian language.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.870
KENNETH: That's that
detail, that's that detail.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:39.080
MARCELLUS: Mm-hmm.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.760
KENNETH: Now look at
these amazing costumes.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.340
Costume designer Ruth
Carter searched the world

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.250
from Ghana to Los Angeles--

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.050
MARCELLUS: OK.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.600
KENNETH: --for textiles and
accessories used to create

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:50.510
the 700 costumes in the film.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.090
Coogler and his team
established a strict color

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:54.540
theme-ing for the film.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.790
For example, blue represented
danger or trouble.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.590
MARCELLUS: Mmm.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.630
KENNETH: So blue was reserved
for the border tribe,

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:00.920
who act as a policing force.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:01.720
MARCELLUS: Mm-hmm.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.740
KENNETH: And Killmonger's
character also wore blue.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.760
No one else is in
any kind of blue.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:06.560
MARCELLUS: That's right.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.727
KENNETH: And the
river tribe right

00:06:07.727 --> 00:06:09.140
here, which is Nakia's tribe--
MARCELLUS: Uh-huh.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.040
KENNETH: --wears green.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:13.490
Lupita Nyong'o, who plays Nakia,
wears many different shades

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.170
of green in her costumes.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:17.330
Carter said greens
mix well together

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:18.990
because it's like nature.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.690
Now, I want to talk about
one of my favorite things

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:21.500
about "Black Panther."

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.420
MARCELLUS: What's that?

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.070
KENNETH: Well with the cast
from all over the world, Coogler

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.500
brought in a dialect
coach to ensure

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.220
there was continuity amongst
all of them. I love that.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.180
That's thinking
through every detail.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.450
MARCELLUS: Mm-hm ]m.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.570
KENNETH: Now, because actor
John Kani's native language

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:42.290
is Xhosa, one of the official
languages of South Africa,

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.280
it became the official
language of Wakanda.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:45.080
MARCELLUS: Yeah.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.420
I really love the celebration
of African culture

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.620
in this movie, Ken.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:50.870
KENNETH: I'm always going to
have memories of my family

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.090
and friends dressing up
in our African attire

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.980
to go and see the
premiere of this film.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:58.370
There was such a sense of
community in the theater,

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.750
and amongst all of us.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.880
And to see these
characters who were

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:04.995
in the comic books come to life
right before our very eyes,

00:07:04.995 --> 00:07:06.380
was powerful.
MARCELLUS: Yeah.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:07.560
KENNETH: Representation matters.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.360
MARCELLUS: It does.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.270
It really does.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.070
And you know what?

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.690
That's our show for today.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.310
Marvel Studios'
"Black Panther" is

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.320
now streaming on Disney+.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:16.910
KENNETH: Wakanda forever.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.670
Chadwick Boseman forever.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.240
MARCELLUS: Forever, indeed.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.950
KENNETH: Until next time,
Kenneth and Marcellus, out.

